 "node": "Convolver",
 "mode": "scene",
 "note": "the impulse response buffer is compared with X_ITE 16.6.0 (channels, length = samples / channels, a sample value), then normalize, the input stage and the clock. Web Audio takes 1, 2 or 4 channels only (3 is not tested: X_ITE throws on it). Runs on the real clock for start and stop. Signal compared with X_ITE 16.6.0 on the page's real Web Audio clock (the source and the Convolver's output as two channels of one recording): with normalize = FALSE a single-sample response of 0.5 gives rms 0.3536 and correlation 1; a response of 0.5 at sample 0 and 0.25 at sample 100 gives the rms of the two summed phasors (computed from the sample rate); a response that is one impulse 441 samples late moves the onset of the tone by 441 samples (10 ms at 44.1 kHz); with normalize = TRUE the output level equals that of a ConvolverNode made on the page with the same response, and X_ITE agrees.",
